{"id":3996,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/was-were/","parentId":540,"order":130,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Was/were: Past simple of ‘be’","seo":{"title":"Was/were: Past simple of 'be' - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use 'was' and 'were' in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1Grammar_Was-were_Past-simple-be.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T17:51:19","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose <em>was/were</em> or <em>am/is/are</em> to complete the following sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"459\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Complete the following sentences with <em>was/were</em> or <em>wasn’t/weren’t</em>.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"460\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write questions using <em>was/were</em> and the words below. Put the words in the correct order.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: you / what time / at the station ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">What time were you at the station</span>?</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"461\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2><strong>Was/were</strong>: Form</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18666\" src=\"/media/uploads/was-were_new.jpg\" alt=\"Grammar chart showing the use of 'was' and 'were' in positive, negative, and question forms, including short answers and common mistakes for the past simple of 'be'.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4><strong>Was/were</strong></h4> <p>We use <strong>was</strong>/<strong>were</strong> as the past simple forms of <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\"><strong>be</strong></a>. We use <strong>was&nbsp;</strong>for<strong>&nbsp;I/he/she/it</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>were&nbsp;</strong>for&nbsp;<strong>you/we/they</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <strong><span>was</span></strong> at home yesterday.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>You <span><strong>were</strong></span> late at the meeting.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>was</strong></span> excited about the party.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>were</strong></span> tired after the excursion.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Were</strong></span> they at the conference?</em></li> </ul> <h4>No positive short forms</h4> <p>The negative short forms of <strong>was not</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>were not</strong> are&nbsp;<strong>wasn’t</strong> and&nbsp;<strong>weren’t</strong>, but there are <strong>no short forms of was&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>were</strong> in affirmative sentences.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Tom <span><strong>was</strong></span> tired, but Susan <span><strong>wasn’t</strong></span> very tired.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>Paul and Tom <span><strong>were</strong></span> happy, but we <span><strong>weren’t</strong></span> happy.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h2><strong>Was/were</strong>: Use</h2> <p><strong>Was</strong>/<strong>were&nbsp;</strong>are the past forms of&nbsp;<strong>am</strong>/<strong>is</strong>/<strong>are</strong>. Present:&nbsp;<strong>am</strong>/<strong>is</strong>&nbsp;= past:&nbsp;<strong>was</strong>. Present:&nbsp;<strong>are&nbsp;</strong>= past:&nbsp;<strong>were</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I<span><strong>‘m</strong></span> happy.</em> ⇒ <em>I <span><strong>was</strong></span> happy.</em> (<strong>am</strong>&nbsp;⇒ <strong>was</strong>)</li> <li><em>She <span><strong>is</strong></span> at her office.</em>&nbsp;⇒ <em>She <span><strong>was</strong></span> at her office.</em>&nbsp;(<strong>is</strong> ⇒ <strong>was</strong>)</li> <li><em>You <span><strong>are</strong></span> late.</em> ⇒ <em>You <span><strong>were</strong></span> late.</em> (<strong>are</strong>&nbsp;⇒ <strong>were</strong>)</li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>was</strong>/<strong>were</strong>&nbsp;to talk about the past. We often use past <a href=\"/vocabulary/a1/time-words-a1-english-vocabulary/\">expressions of time</a>:&nbsp;<strong>yesterday, last night, last week, two months ago, etc</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>She <span><strong>was</strong></span> in Stuttgart last summer. &nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>were</strong></span> late to the party last night.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We use <strong>was</strong>/<strong>were</strong>&nbsp;in the expression&nbsp;<strong>was</strong>/<strong>were born</strong>. The expression&nbsp;<strong>be born</strong> is always past (NOT present):&nbsp;<strong>was/were born</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>‘Where <span><strong>were</strong></span> you born?’ ‘I <span><strong>was</strong></span> born in Sweden.’ <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>‘Where <span><strong>are</strong></span> you born?’ ‘I <span><strong>am</strong></span> born in Sweden.’</em> <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></li> <li><em>Mozart <span><strong>was</strong></span> born in 1756.</em></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <h6>Check the list of all our <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/contents-a1/\">A1 grammar contents</a>.</h6>","quizzes":[{"id":459,"questions":[{"id":4001,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My son <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> short in school, but now he <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> tall. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["was","were"]},{"kind":"select","options":["am","are","is"]}]},{"id":4002,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you at the stadium yesterday?' 'Yes, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Was","Were"]},{"kind":"select","options":["'s","were","was"]}]},{"id":4003,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Yesterday Philip and Emma <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in London. Today they <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> in Paris. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were","was"]},{"kind":"select","options":["is","am","are"]}]},{"id":4004,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sara and I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> at home that night, and you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> with us. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were","was"]},{"kind":"select","options":["were","was"]}]},{"id":4005,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Yesterday we <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> late for the concert, and today I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> late for class. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["was","were"]},{"kind":"select","options":["am","is","are"]}]},{"id":4006,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Asim <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> born in Egypt, and I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> born in Birmingham. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["were","is","was"]},{"kind":"select","options":["am","were","was"]}]},{"id":4007,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you excited about the trip?' 'Yes, we <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> very excited.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Were","Was"]},{"kind":"select","options":["were","'re","was"]}]},{"id":4008,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Kate angry yesterday after the meeting?' 'No, but I think she <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> angry now.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Were","Was"]},{"kind":"select","options":["am","is","are"]}]},{"id":4009,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you at the beach last Sunday?' 'Yes, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Was","Were"]},{"kind":"select","options":["was","were"]}]},{"id":4010,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The weather <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> nice today, but it <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> horrible last weekend. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["are","was","is"]},{"kind":"select","options":["were","was"]}]}]},{"id":460,"questions":[{"id":4011,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Where <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you last night? I called you, but you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> at home. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4022,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Sandra happy after the exam?' 'No, she <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4023,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I remember I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> very worried, but you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> calm. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4024,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Betty and Paul <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> at home; they <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> at the cinema</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4025,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you tired after the concert?' 'Yes, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4026,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I'm very sorry. You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> right, and I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> wrong. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4027,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'Were your parents at the meeting?' 'My dad <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> there, but my mum <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4028,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> late! We <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> early. The concert was at 8 and we arrived at 7. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4029,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Vivian <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> at the meeting, but I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> there. I always go to the meetings. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4030,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> Tim with you?' 'No, only Sally and Peter <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> there with me.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":461,"questions":[{"id":4012,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>the keys / where ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4013,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Robin / why / at the meeting ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4014,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>born / she / when ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4015,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>how expensive / the hotel ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4016,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>why / you / angry ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4017,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>unconscious / I / after the accident ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4018,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>the questions / difficult ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4019,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>the accident / what time ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4020,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>you / how often / in contact with them ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>? </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4021,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>where / you and Tom / last night ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}